{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'Map', title: 'Every camera in Korea,<br>on one map',
  shots: [ { src: shots + '01_map_overview.webp', alt: 'Road cameras across Korea shown on the map', w: 720, h: 1524 } ] }) %}
  <p>Expressway cameras are run by the Korea Expressway Corporation, national highways by MOLIT's ITS, and city streets by each municipality. Cameras from the National Police UTIC, MOLIT's ITS, and the Seoul, Gyeonggi, Busan, Daegu, and Jeju open APIs are merged into one map.</p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li><strong>Expressway · National highway · Urban motorway · Regular road</strong>, each with its own color and icon</li>
    <li>Markers <strong>cluster and thin automatically</strong> with the zoom level</li>
    <li>One-tap switch between <strong>satellite and standard map</strong></li>
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'Live video', title: 'Tap a marker —<br>live video right there', soft: true, flip: true,
  shots: [ { src: shots + '03_video_single.webp', alt: 'Live CCTV video after tapping a marker — Incheon Bridge', w: 720, h: 1524 } ] }) %}
  <p>Tap any marker and live video starts instantly. No external browser, no separate player — it streams inside the app.</p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li>HLS streams — <strong>5–10 minutes</strong> behind real time</li>
    <li><strong>Pinch zoom, drag, double-tap zoom</strong> to control the frame</li>
    <li>Left / right arrows jump to <strong>the next camera on the same road</strong> — watch along the route</li>
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'Nearby', title: 'Several nearby cameras<br>at once',
  shots: [
    { src: shots + '05_nearby_grid.webp', alt: 'Nearby cameras in a 6-split grid', w: 720, h: 1524 },
    { src: shots + '04_nearby_list.webp', alt: 'Nearby cameras in list view — large videos one per row', w: 720, h: 1524 }
  ] }) %}
  <p>The search button at the bottom of the map streams the cameras nearest the current map center, all at the same time — handy for checking your commute route.</p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li><strong>6-split grid</strong> for multi-monitor style watching</li>
    <li><strong>Pinch zoom and pan</strong> on the grid; tap a cell to expand it</li>
    <li>Switch to <strong>list view</strong> for large videos stacked one per row</li>
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'Weather radar', title: 'See where the rain<br>is heading over the road', soft: true, flip: true,
  shots: [ { src: shots + '09_radar.webp', alt: 'Rain radar overlay — precipitation layered over the map', w: 720, h: 1524 } ] }) %}
  <p>The radar button on the right side of the map toggles rain or snow overlays. You see where the rain cloud is moving on top of the road cameras, so the reroute call happens right before you leave.</p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li>Korea Meteorological Administration radar as a <strong>time-lapse animation</strong> over the map</li>
    <li>An <strong>opacity slider</strong> to see roads and precipitation together</li>
    <li><strong>Rain / snow</strong> toggle — read storm zones at a glance</li>
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'Favorites', title: 'Pin the cameras<br>you always watch',
  shots: [ { src: shots + '06_favor.webp', alt: 'Favorites — swipe through saved cameras', w: 720, h: 1524 } ] }) %}
  <p>If there are cameras you check every day on your commute, tap the star once to save them.</p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li>Tap an item and it plays <strong>live in the slot at the top</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Swipe left or right</strong> to cycle through your favorites</li>
    <li>If a camera ID changes, <strong>coordinate-based matching</strong> reconnects the camera at the same spot</li>
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

